      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While increasing your green intake is generally great for heart health, be mindful that some greens, like spinach, contain Vitamin K. Vitamin K can interact with warfarin, potentially affecting its effectiveness. It's best to talk to your doctor or a registered dietitian about how much you should increase your greens while keeping your warfarin dosage stable. They can give you personalized dietary advice to ensure your heart and medication remain safe.",
